From 7e8f9a0b1c2d3e4f5a6b7c8d9e0f1a2b3c4d5e6f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bare Browser <noreply@localhost>
Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 22:56:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 69/70] Add in-browser developer tools and element inspector

Adds mobile developer tools and an interactive DOM element inspector powered by
bundled Eruda, usable directly on device without requiring a remote computer or ADB:

- Long press any page element to choose 'Inspect element' from the context menu,
  instantly highlighting and selecting the exact DOM node in the live inspector tree.
- Adds 'Developer tools' entry point in the main menu to open Console, Network,
  Resources, and Storage inspection.
- Supports Shake-to-Inspect gesture detection (inspired by Andure) to quickly toggle
  the floating developer panel on any webpage.
- Injects via WebContents with browser privileges, ensuring full functionality even on
  pages with strict Content Security Policy (CSP) headers.
